WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.840
The presidential yacht Williamsburg stands by in the Potomac to take aboard the chief

00:09.840 --> 00:16.140
executive for his first extended vacation since taking over the job 16 months ago.

00:16.140 --> 00:22.100
The presidential holiday consists of an offshore cruise north along the New England coast.

00:22.100 --> 00:33.000
Shirt and diet are the main objectives of Mr. Truman's trip.

00:33.000 --> 00:37.800
Aboard the destroyer escort Weiss, 21 White House correspondents keep careful tabs on

00:37.800 --> 00:43.320
the Williamsburg from which they receive telephoned bulletins which are quickly turned into nationwide

00:43.320 --> 00:50.400
copy.

00:50.400 --> 00:54.520
Coming ashore at Quonset, Rhode Island Naval Air Station, the president gives reporters

00:54.520 --> 00:59.980
a firsthand account of his vacation to date and proudly displays a new white yachting

00:59.980 --> 01:06.760
cap made especially for this trip.

01:06.760 --> 01:11.480
Pretty nifty, Mr. President.

01:11.480 --> 01:16.380
Alexander Graham Bell, inventor of the telephone, is again remembered as the 70th anniversary

01:16.380 --> 01:21.600
of the first long-distance call as observed at Paris, Ontario, where this primitive instrument

01:21.600 --> 01:29.120
was used, a far cry to the modern system with its thousands of operators and a myriad of

01:29.120 --> 01:32.120
trunk lines.

01:32.120 --> 01:41.360
A large crowd is present at the anniversary to hear Mayor McCammon of Paris open the ceremonies.

01:41.360 --> 01:45.880
George Dunlop and Reverend Hague took part in that first experiment which covered eight

01:45.880 --> 01:49.400
miles from Brantford to Paris.

01:49.400 --> 01:56.720
As a climax to the ceremony, a plaque is unveiled commemorating the inventor and the history-making

01:56.720 --> 02:06.280
event, a milestone in communication.

02:06.280 --> 02:11.240
Dover's famous castle sees another chapter in its proud history as Winston Churchill,

02:11.240 --> 02:13.940
the new warden of the ports, is installed.

02:13.940 --> 02:24.160
The mayors and barons don their traditional robes for the occasion.

02:24.160 --> 02:29.520
This frontline fortress city turns out wholeheartedly to welcome the great war leader, the Lord

02:29.520 --> 02:35.080
Warden himself, resplendent in his most magnificent uniform.

02:35.080 --> 02:46.160
His wife, son, and daughter Mary attend the ceremonies which demands a proud display.

02:46.160 --> 03:05.680
No one has a better right to guard this symbolic spot.

